Made quite naked; taken from its cover, that it might be used against thine enemies. 

  According to the oaths of the tribes, even thy word; this very difficult clause has been variously translated and explained. According to our version it means, that God employed his bow against the enemies of his people, in accordance with the oaths which he had sworn to the tribes of Israel, promising them protection and deliverance. 

  Didst cleave the earth with rivers;
